# The ACCEPTED side of the #141-residual boundary — the control for
# test/refuse/module_free_read_*.eigs.
#
# The guard refuses a module name that is in the rename set (free-assigned,
# never top-level bound) and READ on a path that can run before its first
# write. Everything here is on the other side of exactly that decision, one
# instance per thing the scan branches on: a plain earlier write; an `if` whose
# BOTH arms write (the meet); a nested `define` that binds the name; a nested
# `define` that reads a name the encloser already bound (the arm that keeps
# lib/ui_w_dialog in the envelope); a write at loop-body depth 0 read later in
# the same body; and — the control that must never enter the rename set at all
# — a free read with no write anywhere, which resolves outward into this
# program (t322's rule, re-asserted here beside its refused neighbours).
#
# Planted fault: delete the `module_freeread_name` guard from splice_module and
# this fixture stays GREEN while the four refuse fixtures go red; break the
# guard the other way (drop the `func`/`assign` binding arms from fr_scan) and
# THIS one goes red as a build refusal. The pair brackets the boundary.
gouter is 100
